---An `NPCList` provides access to all active NPCEntities in the game world, as well as several methods to search for
---entities.
---
---Info: All methods return an array of NPCEntities.
---
---See each method for examples on how to use this list.
---@class NPCList
NPCList = {}

---Returns all active NPCEntities in the game world in an array.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.All() end

---Returns the NPCEntity with the matching UID.
---@param uid integer A valid UID value.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.ByUID(uid) end

---Returns any NPCEntity with a display name matching the given `name` value.
---
---String matches are case-insensitive. Matches are exact unless wildcard characters `?` and/or `*` are provided.
---@param name string The string to match against `NPCEntity.displayName`.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.ByName(name) end

---Returns any NPCEntity within `range` tiles of the given `coordGrid` value.
---
---Exact coord matches should use a value of `0` for `range`.
---@param coordGrid CoordGrid The coord at which to centre the distance search.
---@param range integer The maximum tile distance from the given coord which an NPCEntity must be.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.ByDistance(coordGrid, range) end

---Returns any NPCEntity that uses the given NPCType config.
---
---Info: If the NPCEntity has a valid `NPCEntity.config` then this will test against `NPCEntity.config`. If not, then
---the value for `NPCEntity.parentConfig` will be tested against instead.
---@param npcType NPCType The config to look for when testing NPCEntities.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.ByConfig(npcType) end

---Returns any NPCEntity that uses the given NPCType config ID.
---
---Info: If the NPCEntity has a valid `NPCEntity.config` then this will test against `NPCEntity.configID`. If not, then
---the value for `NPCEntity.parentConfigID` will be tested against instead.
---@param npcTypeID integer The config ID to look for when testing NPCEntities.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.ByConfigID(npcTypeID) end

---Returns any NPCEntity that uses the given NPCType config as its `parentConfig`.
---
---Info: Only `NPCEntity.parentConfig` is tested, while `NPCEntity.config` is not tested against.
---@param npcType NPCType The config to look for when testing NPCEntities.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.ByParentConfig(npcType) end

---Returns any NPCEntity that uses the given NPCType parent config ID.
---
---Info: Only `NPCEntity.parentConfigID` is tested, while `NPCEntity.configID` is not tested against.
---@param npcTypeID integer The config ID to look for when testing NPCEntities.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.ByParentConfigID(npcTypeID) end

---Returns any NPCEntity that matches all tests in the `filterSet` table.
---
---Available tests are:
---
---Tests can be combined as shown below:
---
---Info: Tests are inclusive. All must pass in order for the NPCEntity to be included in the return array.
---@param filterSet NPCListFilterSettings A table of key-value pairs which describe individual tests to perform.
---@return NPCEntity[] # An array of NPCEntities.
function NPCList.Filter(filterSet) end

---The keys `NPCList.Filter` takes in its table.
---@class NPCListFilterSettings
---@field uid integer? A valid entity UID. `{ uid = npcEntity.uid }` See NPCList.ByUID()
---@field name string? A name to match against `NPCEntity.displayName`. `{ name = "*lumbridge*" }` See NPCList.ByName()
---@field coordGrid CoordGrid? A coord to test entity distance from. If `range` is not provided, the default value of `range` will be `0`. `{ coordGrid = CoordGrid._0_50_50_32_32 }` See NPCList.ByDistance()
---@field range integer? Ignored if `coordGrid` key is not provided. `{ range = 4 }` See NPCList.ByDistance()
---@field config NPCType? The config to match against `NPCEntity.config`. `{ config = config.NPC.HANS }` See NPCList.ByConfig()
---@field configID integer? The config ID to match against `NPCEntity.configID`. `{ configID = id.NPC.HANS }` See NPCList.ByConfigID()
---@field parentConfig NPCType? The config to match against `NPCEntity.parentConfig`. `{ parentConfig = config.NPC.THIGUI_ROBIN_MULTI }` See NPCList.ByParentConfig()
---@field parentConfigID integer? The config ID to match against `NPCEntity.parentConfigID`. `{ parentConfigID = id.NPC.THIGUI_ROBIN_MULTI }` See NPCList.ByParentConfigID()
---@field func (fun(npcEntity: NPCEntity): boolean)|nil A function which returns a boolean, and which takes an NPCEntity as its only parameter. This function is called for every entity, and any call that returns `true` will include that NPCEntity in the return array. `function ratFinder(npcEntity) { return npcEntity.config == config.NPC.RAT }` `{ func = ratFinder }`
